<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Brno</h1><p class="st-meta">1054 CE – 1200 CE (approx.) · capital Brno</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">One of the Moravian appanage duchies held by junior Přemyslid princes, centred on Brno, until Moravia was reunited as a margraviate.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bretislaus-i-duke-of-bohemia">Bretislaus I</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bohemia">Bohemia</a> arranged <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/margraviate-of-moravia">Moravia</a> as a domain for junior members of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/premyslid-dynasty">Přemyslid dynasty</a>. After his death in 1055, his sons divided it; Conrad I received the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brno">Brno</a> portion, centred on the castle of Brno (Brünn) in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a>, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olomouc">Olomouc</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/znojmo">Znojmo</a> formed separate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanages</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The princes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brno">Brno</a> owed allegiance to the senior duke in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a> but frequently joined in the dynasty's feuds; Conrad I himself briefly became Duke of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bohemia">Bohemia</a> in 1092. Brno grew as a castle and market centre. Little is known in detail of its administration, which followed the Bohemian castle system.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the late 12th century the Moravian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanages</a> were absorbed. Around 1182 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/margraviate-of-moravia">Moravia</a> was declared a margraviate directly subject to the emperor, and by about 1197 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladislaus-iii-duke-of-bohemia">Vladislaus Henry</a> united the Moravian lands under his rule. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brno">Brno</a> later became the capital of the Margraviate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="duchy, 1054 CE – 1200 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">duchy</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:80.68%;width:2.91%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1054 CE – 1200 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Brno</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Conrad I of Brno, Oldřich of Brno</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Czech</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/czech-republic">Czech Republic</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Brünn, Moravian appanage of Brno</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1127&amp;focus=duchy-of-brno" aria-label="Duchy of Brno on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5063 462 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Brno lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5383 718L5330 692M5383 718L5383 718"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5330 692h0M5383 718h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5383 718h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5383 718h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Brno. <a href="/atlas?year=1127&amp;focus=duchy-of-brno">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
